식당에서는 \"I would like a bag of ",["$","strong","strong-2",{"children":"chips"}],".\" 라고 하면 봉지 과자(포테이토 칩)를 받게 됩니다."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-8 [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6 text-gray-700 font-light text-lg","children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"✅ 예문 (의류):"}],"\r\n영국에서는 \"Your new ",["$","strong","strong-1",{"children":"trousers"}]," look great!\" 라고 말하지만, 미국에서 ",["$","strong","strong-2",{"children":"trousers"}],"는 보통 격식 있는 복장을 의미하며 일상적인 바지는 ",["$","strong","strong-3",{"children":"pants"}],"라고 부릅니다."]}],"\n",["$","h3",null,{"className":"scroll-m-20 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 text-yes-blue","children":"3. 기타 일상용품"}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"className":"my-6 ml-6 list-disc [&>li]:mt-2 marker:text-yes-blue","children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-7 pl-2","children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"쓰레기 / 손전등"}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"className":"my-6 ml-6 list-disc [&>li]:mt-2 marker:text-yes-blue","children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-7 pl-2","children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"영국:"}]," rubbish (쓰레기), torch (손전등)"]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-7 pl-2","children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"미국:"}]," trash or garbage (쓰레기), flashlight (손전등)"]}],"\n"]}],"\n"]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-8 [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6 text-gray-700 font-light text-lg","children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"✅ 예문:"}],"\r\n\"The power is out, so please grab the ",["$","strong","strong-1",{"children":"torch"}]," from the cupboard.\" (영국)\r\n\"The power is out, so please grab the ",["$","strong","strong-2",{"children":"flashlight"}]," from the cupboard.\" (미국)"]}],"\n",["$","hr","hr-2",{}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"className":"scroll-m-20 border-b border-gray-100 pb-2 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight first:mt-0 mt-12 mb-6 text-gray-900","children":"문법(Grammar): 완료 시제와 전치사 사용의 미묘한 경계"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"class